*.fq
*.fq.gz
*.bam
*.bai
*.cram
*.sam
*.vcf.gz
*.bcf
*.h5
*.h5ad
*.npz

# --------------------------------- third-party source material (COPYRIGHTED)
# Papers, vendor manuals, supplementary tables, and anything derived from
# them by extraction: text dumps, screenshots, spreadsheets. None of it is
# ours to redistribute. Every source is cited in the notes by DOI or by
# document number and revision, so it can be re-obtained from the
# publisher or vendor -- and what we computed FROM it lives in the models
# and self-tests, which is the point of this repo: the derived facts are
# checked and citable without shipping the source document.
*.pdf
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.doc
*.docx
*.pptx

# extracted or scanned material: page text, figures, gel photographs
*.txt
# ...but these conventional text files are ours, not extracted from anything
!requirements.txt
!requirements-*.txt
!LICENSE.txt
!CITATION.txt
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.gif
*.tif
*.tiff

# correspondence: private as well as third-party
email*.txt

# plasmid maps and sequence deposits: other people's deposited data, redistributed by
# Addgene or SnapGene under their own terms (Addgene put sequence data behind a login in
# October 2025 for exactly this reason). Each ref/MANIFEST.md names the Addgene ID, and
# the self-tests skip the checks that read them.
*.dna
*.gb
*.gbk
*.fa
*.fasta

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# ------------------------------------------------------------ generated HTML
# Every .html in the repo is output: the protocol pages come from each
# <protocol>/tools/build_page.py, the note pages and notes.html from
# build_docs.py, and index.html from build_index.py. Rebuild with:
#     for b in */tools/build_page.py; do python3 "$b"; done
#     python3 build_docs.py && python3 build_index.py
# Keeping it out of the index keeps diffs readable -- a one-line sequence change
# otherwise rewrites thousands of lines of aligned diagram. If a published site
# is wanted later, build it in CI from the sources rather than committing it.
*.html
# No exceptions: the archived upstream exemplar (ref/SPLiT-seq.html) is
# somebody else's page, so it stays local and is not redistributed here.

# The assembled website (build_site.py): rebuilt in CI by .github/workflows/pages.yml
# and deployed to GitHub Pages, never committed.
_site/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, for the record:
#   <protocol>/ref/   -- archived third-party reference (vendor tables, barcode
#                        whitelists, Addgene maps); small, and the notes are
#                        unverifiable without them.

# the catalogue's download cache: third-party HTML, re-fetchable, never committed
catalogue/tools/.cache/

# downloaded / derived data -- never committed, see "Data policy" in README.md
_data/
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq
*.fq.gz
*.bam
*.sam
*.counts.tsv

# papers and anything extracted from them -- source material, not code
pdf/
